.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines containing a search string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.br
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep
function searches the file pointed to by
.BR fp
for lines containing the string pointed to by
.BR search_str .

For every matching line, the function stores a dynamically allocated copy
of the line in the array pointed to by
.BR matches .

The function returns the number of matching lines. It returns -1 if an
input pointer is NULL or if memory allocation fails.

The caller is responsible for freeing the memory allocated for the
matching lines and the matches array.

